    "Paragraph 3 argues that vague guarantees are 'a deliberate instrument' that makes both partner and adversary careful. The island case, where the great power 'declines to say' whether the promise covers a dispute the partner starts, illustrates this, and the author stresses that 'The silence is not an oversight.'",
    "Reading the example as evidence from history, or as a failure, when it is a hypothetical illustration of deliberate policy.",
