rcq("R04-E-08-3", "Application / analogy", "Medium",
    "Which of the following situations is most closely analogous to the dilemma described in paragraph 2?",
    "A parent's promise to pay all of a grown child's debts reassures but invites borrowing; withholding it curbs borrowing but leaves the child feeling deserted.",
    [("A shopkeeper who offers a generous guarantee on every item she stocks sells more goods but must then pay to repair the ones that break.",
      "This is a single trade-off between sales and repair costs; there is no protected party whose conduct is emboldened by assurance and restrained by doubt."),
     ("An employer who keeps the terms of a bonus vague so that staff keep working hard without counting on any fixed reward.",
      "This parallels the deliberate ambiguity of paragraph 3, a response to the dilemma, rather than the dilemma of paragraph 2 itself."),
     ("A teacher who sets a very difficult examination finds that the strongest students in the class rise to it while the weakest ones simply give up.",
      "This describes different reactions of different students to one measure, not one relationship in which easing one risk aggravates another.")],
    "Paragraph 2 says tightening a commitment reassures the partner but 'may embolden' it, while loosening it restrains the partner but invites doubt. The parent's open-ended promise reassures but encourages risky borrowing, and withholding it restrains but leaves the child doubting support: easing one problem worsens the other.",
    "Choosing the vague-bonus case because it resembles the alliance discussion, though it matches paragraph 3, not paragraph 2.",
    "Two analogies share surface features with the passage; only one reproduces the two-sided structure of paragraph 2.",
    cognitive="Application")

